  "detail": "the sandbox as configured was observed in Chromium 148.0.7778.96. Generated scripts ran inside it (inline and admitted asset); the document is an opaque origin with no cookie, storage, IndexedDB, parent DOM or opener; the sandbox refused top navigation, popups and form submission; the served policy refused every subresource outside the admitted assets (0 host-API and 0 external-sink requests, refusals on the console); permissions are denied with 0 parser warnings; admitted assets loaded, including a CORS-mode image. The frame navigated itself three ways -- a link, the page's own script, and a meta refresh the page inserted (one document is served, so that tag is inserted by the page's script) -- which MIK-R104 v2 accepts as a channel (D331): each is observed and named here, none is a failed boundary, and none gained a write. The matrix exercised all eight load classes against four foreign targets (previous revision, sibling frame, task path and known live sibling session), plus three own-asset controls. Fonts used FontFace.load(); media decode errors alone were not proof: any foreign HTTP 200 fails. 8 live sibling-session classes were asserted; 0 loaded.  Disposal: the document's interval stopped when the page closed and a revoked channel answered 410. Not contained and not claimed: a live frame's timers have no enforced count, and its heap and CPU/GPU have no browser-enforced ceiling; no stronger container is built (rule 8, D331)."
